{"r":"sxT","lane":{"p":1324,"e":[{"h":"سَخِطَ","t":["aor. , inf. n. ",[2,"سَخَطٌ"]," (S, * Msb, K *) [and ",[2,"مَسْخَطٌ"],", (see ",[2,"سُخْطٌ"],", below,)] ",[1,"He was,"]," or ",[1,"became, displeased,"]," or ",[1,"discontented;"]," (S, * K, TA;) as also ↓ ",[2,"تسخّط"],"; (K, TA;) syns. ",[2,"كَرِهَ"]," and ",[2,"تَكَرَّهَ"]," [the latter of which, app. referring particularly to ↓ ",[2,"تسخّط"],", properly and generally signifies, when intrans., ",[1,"he expressed,"]," or ",[1,"showed, dislike, displeasure, disapprobation, discontent,"]," or ",[1,"hatred"],"]: (TA:) ",[1,"he was,"]," or ",[1,"became, angry;"]," (S, Msb, TA;) and ↓ ",[2,"تسخّط"]," signifies ",[1,"the same;"]," or ",[1,"he became angered;"]," syn. ",[2,"تَغَضَّبَ"],". (TA.) You say, ",[2,"سَخِطَ عَلَيْهِ"]," [",[1,"He was,"]," or ",[1,"became, displeased,"]," or ",[1,"discontented,"]," or ",[1,"angry, with him"],"]. (Kur v. 83.) And ",[2,"سَخِطَهُ"],[1,"He was,"]," or ",[1,"became, displeased,"]," or ",[1,"discontented, with him;"]," as also ↓ ",[2,"تسخّطهُ"],"; both expl. by ",[2,"لَمْ"],[2,"يَرْضَ بِهِ"],"; (Ham p. 502;) and the latter by ",[2,"تَكَرَّهَهُ"]," [which signifies as above, like ",[2,"كَرِهَهُ"],", and also ",[1,"he expressed,"]," or ",[1,"showed, dislike of it, displeasure with it, disapprobation of it, discontent with it,"]," or ",[1,"hatred of it"],"]; (K, TA;) and ",[2,"لَمْ يَرْضَهُ"],"; (TA;) as in the saying, ↓ ",[2,"كُلَّمَا عَمِلْتُ لَهُ عَمَلًا تَسَخَّطَهُ"]," [",[1,"Every time that I did for him a deed, he expressed,"]," or ",[1,"showed, dislike of it,"]," &c.]; and in like manner, ↓ ",[2,"أَعْطَاهُ قَلِيلًا فَتَسَخَّطَهُ"]," [",[1,"He gave him little and he expressed,"]," or ",[1,"showed, dislike of it,"]," &c.]: (TA:) and [hence,] ",[2,"عَطَآءَهُ"]," ↓ ",[2,"تَسَخَّطَ"],[1,"He deemed his gift little, and it did not stand with him in any stead;"]," expl. by ",[2,"اِسْتَقَلَّهُ وَلَمْ يَقَعْ مِنْهُ"],[2,"مَوْقِعًا"],". (S, K.) You say also, ",[2,"اَللّٰهُ يَسْخَطُ لَكُمْ كَذَا"],", meaning ",[1,"God forbiddeth you such a thing:"]," or ",[1,"will punish you for such a thing:"]," or it may refer to the desire of punishing for it. (TA.)"],"f":"1"},{"h":"اسخطهُ","t":["[",[1,"He displeased,"]," or ",[1,"discontented, him:"],"] ",[1,"he angered him; made him angry."]," (S, Msb, K.)"],"f":"4"},{"h":"تَسَخَّطَ","t":["see 1, in seven places."],"f":"5"},{"h":"سُخْطٌ","t":["(S, Msb, K,) a subst. from ",[2,"سَخِطَ"],", (Msb,) ",[1,"Dislike, displeasure, disapprobation,"]," or ",[1,"discontent;"]," (TA;) ",[1,"contr. of"],[2,"رِضًى"],"; (S, K, TA;) as also ↓ ",[2,"سُخُطٌ"]," (Sgh, K) and ↓ ",[2,"سَخَطٌ"]," (S, K) and ↓ ",[2,"مَسْخَطٌ"],": (Sgh, K:) [the last two of which are inf. ns.:] ",[1,"anger;"]," (Msb;) as also ↓ ",[2,"سَخَطٌ"],". (TA.)"]},{"h":"سَخَطٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"سُخْطٌ"],", in two places."]},{"h":"سُخُطٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"سُخْطٌ"],"."]},{"h":"سَاخِطٌ","t":["[",[1,"Displeased; discontented:"],"] ",[1,"angry."]," (S.)"]},{"h":"مَسْخَطٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"سُخْطٌ"],"."]},{"h":"مَسْخَطَةٌ","t":["[",[1,"A cause,"]," or ",[1,"means,"]," or ",[1,"an occasion, of dislike, displeasure, disapprobation,"]," or ",[1,"discontent:"]," and, ",[1,"of anger:"]," or ",[1,"a cause,"]," &c., ",[1,"of procuring dislike,"]," &c.: pl., app., ",[2,"مَسَاخِطُ"]," and ",[2,"مَسَاخِطَةٌ"],". Hence the saying,] ",[2,"البِرُّ مَرْضَاةٌ لِلرَّبِّ مَسْخَطَةٌ لِلشَّيْطَانِ"]," [",[1,"Piety is a cause of approbation to the Lord; a cause of disapprobation,"]," or ",[1,"anger, to the devil"],"]. (TA.)"]},{"h":"مَسْخُوطٌ","t":[[1,"Disliked, disapproved,"]," or ",[1,"hated:"]," (A, K:) in this sense applied to a gift. (A, TA.) You say also, ",[2,"هُوَ مَسْخُوطٌ عَلَيْهِ"],[1,"He is an object of anger."]," (TA.) ― -b2- [Hence,] ",[1,"Transformed,"]," or ",[1,"metamorphosed, into a worse,"]," or ",[1,"more foul,"]," or ",[1,"more ugly, shape:"]," [and hence applied by the Arabs in the present day to any idol or other image of ancient workmanship; such being regarded by them as metamorphosed in consequence of having incurred the wrath of God:] and ",[1,"short:"]," but thus applied, it is a vulgar term. (TA.)"]}]},"mufradat":["السخط والسخط: الغضب الشديد المقتضي للعقوبة، قال: إذا هم يسخطون [التوبة/ 58] ، وهو من الله تعالى: إنزال العقوبة، قال تعالى: ذلك بأنهم اتبعوا ما أسخط الله [محمد/ 28] ، أن سخط الله عليهم [المائدة/ 80] ، كمن باء بسخط من الله [آل عمران/ 162] ."]}